problem_statement:
Assignment to identifier in namespace is incorrectly transpiled
### Describe the bug

When transpiling code with a TS namespace to module=ESM + target=es2017, the namespace is missing in the `AssignmentExpression`.

### Input code

```typescript
namespace API {
  export let url = '/'

  export function update(value: string) {
    url = value
  }
}

API.update('/new')
console.log(API.url)
```


### Config

```json
{
"sourceMaps": true,
  "jsc": {
    "parser": {
      "syntax": "typescript",
      "tsx": true,
      "decorators": true
    },
    "target": "es2017",
    "loose": false,
    "externalHelpers": true,
    "keepClassNames": false
  },
  "module": {
    "type": "es6"
  },
  "minify": false
}
```


### Playground link

https://play.swc.rs/?version=1.3.89&code=H4sIAAAAAAAAA0WMOwrDMBAF%2Bz3F62Q1dh9wkTJdriCUjTFsdoU%2BSSD47jHC4PK9YUbDi0sKkXG93%2FAjgL%2FJcoVwRcuCGW5ydP7PprGupmjpESoP7yCNLyg1r7r4XsAhdrTvjTaiPT8eipuUP85TNC0mPIotQ8dZ%2FB%2BWWPhrkAAAAA%3D%3D&config=H4sIAAAAAAAAA1VPQQ6CQAy88wrSMwf1oIlXL170D80yGnRhN21JIIS%2FuyiI3joznZl2yEhDKw4XjkrH3KRFkeU5PdQlOKQxgciikC9OjPaNcZcYsj5CnVTRqFhU0%2B4n602VcEHYgiwtb2H86GQsd9gUB91ttoc5inwIikTf2OucRegM0rA%2Fw0eI%2FhXRE4gnz6pXrqGLM5ubqA5l67E%2BNh3%2Fad3TulQ11a3%2FescX%2FL2OKyQBAAA%3D

### SWC Info output

_No response_

### Expected behavior

[tsc](https://www.typescriptlang.org/play?#code/HYQwtgpgzgDiDGEAEBBACgSSQbwFBKQgA8YB7AJwBckAbCagV3JqQF4kByAeg930JIVqAMwbB4lAJalgSBjAAmIShAAUANxA0GEAFxIolcpOABzAJQ5+BJi3abtEfgF9cr3OgwA6eUpWruYAgAdw5zXHgZKFI6LxpSU1VPH2ZzIA) generates:
```js
"use strict";
var API;
(function (API) {
    API.url = '/';
    function update(value) {
        API.url = value;   // <-- note the "API."
    }
    API.update = update;
})(API || (API = {}));
API.update('/new');
console.log(API.url);
```

### Actual behavior

SWC generates:

```js
var API;
(function(API) {
    API.url = '/';
    function update(value) {
        url = value;   // <-- invalid
    }
    API.update = update;
})(API || (API = {}));
API.update('/new');
console.log(API.url);
```

### Version

1.3.89

### Additional context

_No response_

